# What tools/bench/Dockerfile is built from, as an allowlist: everything is left
# out, then the files the image needs are let back in. tools/bench_in_container.py
# builds from a copy of the committed tree and puts this file at that copy's
# root as both .dockerignore and .containerignore, so Docker and Podman read the
# same list. BuildKit also finds it here, beside the Dockerfile.
**
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!MANIFEST.in
!requirements
!src
!tests
# A directory let back in admits its whole subtree, and not only itself: the
# matcher un-ignores a path when a pattern matches that path or any of its
# parents, and the trailing slash is dropped before the comparison. So a bare
# `!tools/` let the entire tools tree into the context and made the leaves under
# it redundant, which is not the allowlist this file opens by claiming to be.
# Each directory on the way to a file the image needs is therefore let back in
# and then emptied again, and the leaves after it are the whole of what these two
# trees contribute. `tools/bench/Dockerfile` and this file are not among them:
# the build reads the Dockerfile through `--file` and bench_in_container.py copies
# this list to the context root itself.
!build-inputs
build-inputs/*
!build-inputs/cubeprogrammer.zip
!build-inputs/cubeclt.zip
!tools
tools/*
!tools/bench
tools/bench/*
!tools/bench/install_cubeprogrammer.sh
!tools/bench/cubeprogrammer-auto-install.xml
!tools/bench/extract_cubeclt.py
# The tier copies, builds and flashes this demo, and builds its own images out
# of it.
!examples/nucleo-f446re_demo
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
examples/nucleo-f446re_demo/build
examples/nucleo-f446re_demo/.agentic-hil
